		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">58</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As there are 1000 elements in the array, it will be difficult for me to remember all the elements of the array, so I will write all the elements of the array in paper.
2. It will be dificult for me to remember the length of current and previous strictly increasing sub array, so that also i will write in paper.
3. Also I have keep track of start index and end index of the sub array, so I have to write that also in paper.
4. Now after I reach to elements when the current element of array is smalller than previous element then i will update the update the current start index, since all sub array will have differnt start index and also i will write the end index of current sub array that I have.
5. When I reach the element which is smaller than previous element than I have to compare the length of current sub array with the previous sub array I have and according to that I have to update start Index and end index of the largest strictly increasing sub array. </attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">1449.1275246785046</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">5015.242518579472</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">377.5226057000692</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">287.47824261708035</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As there are 1000 elements in the array, it will be difficult for me to remember all the elements of the array, so I will write all the elements of the array in paper.
2. It will be dificult for me to remember the length of current and previous strictly increasing sub array, so that also i will write in paper.
3. Also I have keep track of start index and end index of the sub array, so I have to write that also in paper.
4. Now after I reach to elements when the current element of array is smalller than previous element then i will update the update the current start index, since all sub array will have differnt start index and also i will write the end index of current sub array that I have.
5. When I reach the element which is smaller than previous element than I have to compare the length of current sub array with the previous sub array I have and according to that I have to update start Index and end index of the largest strictly increasing sub array. </attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentWidth" type="double">377.5226057000692</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentHeight" type="double">262.59375</attribute>
